# shellcheck -S warning findings frozen per (file, code) over lint-shell.sh's file set.
# Format: <file> | SC<code> | <count> | <reason>   (the reason is the rest of the line)
# The four-way rule applies: a new pair, a higher count, an unrecorded lower count
# and a row whose pair is gone all FAIL. Record a fix with --write-baseline [--files f].
# Every row carries a verdict. `F4 2026-09-04` is provenance -- the review pass that
# wrote them; that backlog track is CLOSED and its residue is backlog CL6.
# docs/code-quality-tooling.md#shellcheck-warning-ratchet-shellcheck-warnings
linux/host-config/ghcr-prune-package.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `created` is the THIRD tab field of candidates.tsv and exists to consume the column. With `read -r vid digest` the tab and the timestamp land inside digest and the failure log prints a mangled digest. The dry-run branch reads the same column as awk $3.
linux/scripts/01-core/artifact-common.sh | SC1090 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: the path is `${_ARTIFACT_COMMON_DIR}/${_ac_module}` over a runtime module list, so no literal `# shellcheck source=` exists. Coverage is verify-script-copy-coverage.py plus the suites that source the modules for real.
linux/scripts/01-core/cross-apt.sh | SC2120 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: apt_update_smart is a PUBLIC helper with an optional argv (it defaults to -y). SC2120 only reports that no in-tree caller passes extra args today; the parameter is contract, not dead code.
linux/scripts/01-core/cross-env-doctor.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `failures` is passed BY NAME to all four _doctor_phase_* helpers, each of which binds it with `local -n` and appends. Deleting it would leave every phase's nameref dangling.
linux/scripts/01-core/cross-env.sh | SC2206 | 1 | KEEP, sharpened CL6 2026-09-05: CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM is operator-reachable (build-litert.sh exports it), so quoting is NOT a no-op -- it would collapse a multi-word value into one argv word. Six other sites already pass the same variable quoted; whether that disagreement can ever bite is a cmake-argv question only a build answers, and neither reading is subtraction.
linux/scripts/01-core/runtime-build-fns.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `parent_context_dir` is the 4th positional of _runtime_resolve_parent_context, which writes it through a nameref. The `local` is what gives the nameref a target in this frame.
linux/scripts/02-toolchain/python/build_python.sh | SC1090 | 2 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: the same two-layout bootstrap as base-image.sh, plus a pkg-config fixup sourced only when present. Both paths are chosen at runtime.
linux/scripts/02-toolchain/verify-gcc.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `local PREFIX=$1` is unused ON PURPOSE — the function verifies the ACTIVE gcc on PATH, not a prefix tree, and the local also shields the caller's global PREFIX from the function. It documents the arity build-gcc.sh:846 calls with; drop it only together with that call site.
linux/scripts/03-media/build/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-probe-framework.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `out_ref` is the caller's nameref; the line already carries a scoped SC2206 disable explaining the deliberate IFS re-split. The SC2034 is the same nameref blind spot.
linux/scripts/03-media/build/gstreamer/common/pre-setup.sh | SC2120 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: _apt_refresh takes optional apt args exactly like cross-apt.sh's apt_update_smart; same verdict.
linux/scripts/03-media/runtime/install-deps.sh | SC2046 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: word splitting is the mechanism — the dpkg-grep-awk pipeline yields one package name per line and apt-get purge needs them as separate argv words. Debian package names cannot contain whitespace or glob characters.
linux/scripts/03-media/runtime/media-env.sh | SC2034 | 4 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP — the warning is simply WRONG here: the whole block sits between `set -a` and `set +a`, so every assignment is exported. shellcheck does not model allexport. Adding `export` per line would be redundant and would invite someone to move a line out of the block.
linux/scripts/04-runtime/entrypoint.sh | SC1090 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: sources every *.sh the image drops in the env.d directory — the whole point is that the set is not known statically. Narrowing it to a fixed list would break the drop-in contract.
linux/scripts/04-runtime/verify-runtime-paths.sh | SC1090 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: sources the generated paths env file it exists to VERIFY; a static directive would check the generator's template instead of the artifact.
linux/scripts/build-cross-chain.sh | SC2046 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `$(arch_list_to_words ...)` exists to turn a comma list into argv words for run_parallel_arch_loop; quoting it would pass all three arches as ONE argument and the loop would build a bogus arch.
linux/scripts/build-runtime-artifacts.sh | SC2046 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: same arch_list_to_words splitting contract as build-cross-chain.sh.
linux/scripts/build-runtime-manifest.sh | SC2046 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: same arch_list_to_words splitting contract as build-cross-chain.sh.
linux/scripts/build-sdk-artifacts.sh | SC2046 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: same arch_list_to_words splitting contract as build-cross-chain.sh.
linux/scripts/lib/agentic-loop.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: MATRIX_BUILD_TYPE is reset then re-assigned by the eval of the jq-generated assignments at :566; the documented consumer set is listed at :551. The reset is what makes a missing jq field empty instead of stale.
linux/scripts/lib/code-quality.sh | SC2034 | 2 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: both are the library's documented OUT variables (see the comments at :215 and :247) — the consumer is the CI caller that sources this file, never the file itself.
linux/scripts/tests/test-ancestry.sh | SC2034 | 3 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: all three are INPUTS to the function under test, read from the sourced module — CROSS_STAGE_ORDER by the stage-defs walkers, CROSS_RUN_ID by append_runtime_image_output, and RUNTIME_ANDROID_PIN_arm64 indirectly via runtime_android_pin_varname (tag-naming.sh:80), which is why no literal reference exists anywhere.
linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | SC2034 | 5 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: fixture state read by the chain functions under test — CROSS_LOG_ARCHIVE_KEEP by the log archiver, PARALLEL_ARCHS by the lane gate, FINAL_IMAGE/TARGET_ARCHES and CROSS_STAGE_ORDER by the stage walkers.
linux/scripts/tests/test-chain-lifecycle.sh | SC2163 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: `export "$@"` in _lane_run forwards the case's VAR=VAL knobs into a subshell; the subshell is what keeps them from leaking into the next case.
linux/scripts/tests/test-cli-parsers.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: ORCHESTRATOR_UNSUPPORTED_FLAGS is the parser's input (cli-parsers.sh:85); the case sets it empty to exercise the no-unsupported-flags arm.
linux/scripts/tests/test-disk-guard.sh | SC2034 | 2 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: CROSS_STAGE_ORDER and TARGET_ARCHES are the fixture the disk guard sizes its lane from.
linux/scripts/tests/test-embedded-python-extract.sh | SC2046 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: the case feeds the whole real tree to the extractor as argv words — the same deliberate split lint-python.sh:66 performs, which is what makes this an honest end-to-end case.
linux/scripts/tests/test-guard-helpers.sh | SC2034 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: SUDO is run_priv's only input and is set inside the subshell that sources common.sh, so the assignment must come after the source and cannot be seen as a read here.
linux/scripts/tests/test-iree-wheelhouse-stages.sh | SC2034 | 3 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: BUILD_PYTHON, MAX_JOBS and IREE_REF are the wheel builder's inputs, read by build_iree_wheels from the sourced module.
linux/scripts/tests/test-iree-wheelhouse-stages.sh | SC2123 | 1 | F4 2026-09-04 reviewed, KEEP: overriding PATH is the POINT of the case — a subshell PATH holding only the stub dir is what makes the cmake-absent guard reachable at all (the case used to pass against the real /usr/bin cmake).
